\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Operational trade-offs across temporal decision methods. Lower false-alert rates and higher recall are preferable; the log-scale $z$-axis encodes per-frame filter runtime ($\mu $s). The dashed line marks the low-compute operating frontier. M2 achieves the fewest false alerts; M3 and M4 share the same recall-preserving operating point. M5's statistically indistinguishable gain over M2 comes at a much larger compute cost.}}{4}{}\protected@file@percent }
